 *     }
 *
 * This computes, for every fixed (r,q), a 1×NP vector–matrix product:
 *
 *   A_out[r][q][p] = sum_{s} A[r][q][s] * C4[s][p]
 *
 * The straightforward translation above:
 *   - Re-reads A[r][q][s] for every p (NP times),
 *   - Walks C4 by columns C4[s][p] (bad locality, strided access),
 *   - Initializes sum[p] inside the p-loop.
 *
 * The optimized version below keeps the arithmetic for each sum[p]
 * in the same order over s (so each individual reduction sees the
 * same sequence of adds), but reorganizes the loop nest as:
 *
 *   for (r)
 *     for (q) {
 *       // 1) zero whole sum-vector once
 *       for (p) sum[p] = 0;
 *       // 2) traverse C4 row-by-row
 *       for (s) {
