 *  - The inner accumulation now iterates s outer, p inner.
 *    * C4[s][p] is laid out with p as the innermost index, so this
 *      accesses each row of C4 contiguously and is cache-friendly.
 *    * A[r][q][s] is loaded once per (r,q,s) and reused across all p.
 *    * sum[p] is updated in a contiguous fashion.
 *  - The order of additions for each (r,q,p) over s is unchanged:
 *      s = 0, 1, ..., NP-1, as in the original kernel; only operations
 *      for different p values are interleaved.
 *
 * Additionally, a compile-time tunable blocking factor along the p
 * dimension is provided via the template parameter P_BLOCK. When
 * P_BLOCK == 0 (default), no explicit blocking is used. For P_BLOCK > 0,
 * the p dimension is processed in blocks of size P_BLOCK using views
 * created with noarr::slice<'p'>. This allows tuning for particular
 * cache hierarchies without changing the call site:
 *
 *   kernel_doitgen<128>(A.get_ref(), C4.get_ref(), sum.get_ref());
